\f0\fs48 \cf0 Goal\
\
To create an interactive webpage with a playable Diagonal 3D Chess.\
\
Take my old 3D chess program, made in Director, and make a functional version that works in the browser. Take my old 3D Chess website and remake it with today\'92s standards, to work both online and off. This includes all pieces, rendered in 3D, from my website (https://thehinge.net/3dchess). \
\
Can you take all the functionality of the old Director file and make a browser version that is rendered in three.js with models built in Blender?\
\
Can you make a game-studio.html file that shows each 3D asset and their chess moves, as well as the board itself? This is a tool for me to be able to view and edit each asset.\
\
I would like the user to be able to:\
- spin, zoom, and pan around the board\
- select pieces, which then show their available moves, and then click an available spot to move them\
- change the way available moves are rendered, between full cubes to simply glowing dots at the center of the cubic move space.\
- save their game. This downloads a .txt file that records the current state of the board.\
- load a game. Upload a .txt file to set the pieces up in a specific way\
\
\
